From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: macbox <macbox@localhost>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 05:57:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 32/33] staged zero page-ups: a texture's first prepare over
 guest pages of zeros writes nothing

A new texture's host texture reads zero before any command (the runtime's FirstMove), and
before its first prepare no GPU work reached it. So when that first prepare's guest pages all
read zero, the page-up (buffer, copy, blit) changes nothing and is skipped. The pages are
scanned a page at a time and the scan stops at the first non-zero page; covered pages take
the view as before. PagedTexture::prepared_once is set by every prepare, synchronize and
skipped Private page-up.

Switch: REIMS_VGPU_STAGED_ZERO=<path>, live while the file exists and page-ups are staged.
The staged log line now splits walk, scan, buffer and copy time and counts all-zero copies.
